From 65955bd201f00641422bced5d65c461d36c5dd33 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Arena Agent <agent@arena.ai>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 08:30:51 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(security): remove published credentials, require auth,
 verify TLS, Postgres-only

The repository is public and carried a working production configuration:

  - README.md published the deploy's real JWT_SECRET, so anyone could sign an
    admin token and write to /api/data.
  - server.js fell back to ADMIN_PASSWORD = 'RuliLab@2026' when the variable
    was unset, so the password was the one in the README.

Nothing has a usable default any more. The server exits with a named reason if
JWT_SECRET (<32 chars, or a previously published value), ADMIN_PASSWORD_HASH
(not bcrypt) or DATABASE_URL is missing.

Also:
  - GET /api/data had no authRequired: the whole register was readable by
    anyone with the URL. It now requires a bearer token, as every other route
    already did.
  - cors({origin:true, credentials:true}) reflected any Origin while
    ALLOWED_ORIGIN was computed and never used; CORS is now an explicit
    allowlist and ALLOWED_ORIGIN is required.
  - ssl: {rejectUnauthorized:false} defeated sslmode=require; TLS is verified.
  - the JSON-file fallback accepted writes on an ephemeral disk and lost them
    at the next deploy while /api/health said ok. Postgres is now required and
    an unreachable database is a startup failure.
  - OTP and alert email interpolated purpose/otp/text straight into HTML; they
    are escaped, and send errors no longer return the provider message.
  - bcrypt.compare is async (the sync call blocked the event loop), login has
    its own 20/15min bucket, malformed JSON returns 400 not 500, and SIGTERM
    drains the pool instead of cutting a write in half.

Routes move to app.js as a factory taking pool + mailer, so they are testable
with no database. Adds npm test (21 tests, including regressions for the public
data route, the reflecting CORS and the unescaped email), a CI workflow that
also fails on a committed credential, npm run secret and npm run hash so no
value ever needs to be written down, .gitignore, and a README that documents
the API instead of a deploy transcript.
