+# Ruli Lab Systems — API server
+
+Small Express service behind the Lab Systems console. It stores the register in
+Postgres and sends the department's transactional email (OTP codes and expiry /
+maintenance reminders).
+
+- Live: `https://lab-server-7hwd.onrender.com`
+- Health: `GET /api/health`
+
+---
+
+## What it does
+
+| Method | Path | Auth | Purpose |
+| --- | --- | --- | --- |
+| `GET` | `/` | — | Name, version, readiness |
+| `GET` | `/api/health` | — | Database reachability, key count, email status |
+| `POST` | `/api/login` | — | Exchange the admin password for a 30-day JWT |
+| `GET` | `/api/data?key=lab/v1` | Bearer | Read the register |
+| `PUT` | `/api/data?key=lab/v1` | Bearer | Replace the register (keeps the previous copy in `history`) |
+| `POST` | `/api/send-otp` | Bearer | Email a one-time code |
+| `POST` | `/api/send-alert` | Bearer | Email a consumable-expiry or equipment reminder |
+
+Every route except `/`, `/api/health` and `/api/login` requires
+`Authorization: Bearer <token>`.
+
+---
+
+## Configuration
+
+All configuration is environment variables. `.env.example` lists them with
+placeholders; nothing in this repository contains a working credential.
+
+### Required
+
+| Variable | Notes |
+| --- | --- |
+| `JWT_SECRET` | ≥32 chars. `npm run secret` |
+| `ADMIN_PASSWORD_HASH` | bcrypt hash. `npm run hash -- "long password"` |
+| `DATABASE_URL` | Postgres URL with `sslmode=require` (Neon free tier is fine) |
+| `ALLOWED_ORIGIN` | Comma-separated allowlist, e.g. `https://ssamahan.github.io` |
+
+The server **exits on startup** if any of these is missing, if `JWT_SECRET` is
+shorter than 32 characters or matches a previously published value, or if
+`DATABASE_URL` cannot be reached. This is deliberate: a server that boots with a
+default secret, or that silently falls back to a file on an ephemeral disk, loses
+data and gives no warning.
+
+### Optional
+
+`ADMIN_USERNAME` (default `admin`), `PGPOOL_MAX` (default `5`), `EMAIL_HOST`,
+`EMAIL_PORT`, `EMAIL_USER`, `EMAIL_PASS`, `EMAIL_FROM`.
+
+---
+
+## Deploy on Render
+
+1. **Environment** → add the four required variables. Generate them locally:
+   ```bash
+   npm install
+   npm run secret
+   npm run hash -- "a long password you will keep in a password manager"
+   ```
+2. Set `DATABASE_URL` to the Neon connection string (include `sslmode=require`).
+3. Set `ALLOWED_ORIGIN` to the console's origin.
+4. Deploy. Watch the log for `✅ Using Postgres — persistent`.
+
+If the log shows `FATAL:`, the service will exit rather than serve in a degraded
+state — read the named variable and set it.
+
+---
+
+## Local development
+
+```bash
+npm install
+cp .env.example .env      # fill in the four required values
+npm test                  # no database or network needed
+npm run dev
+```
+
+The tests stub `pg` and `nodemailer`, so they run with no infrastructure.
+
+---
+
+## Security notes
+
+- **No default credentials.** The password is stored only as a bcrypt hash, and
+  the JWT secret only in the host's environment.
+- **Rotating the password:** `npm run hash -- "new password"`, replace
+  `ADMIN_PASSWORD_HASH`, redeploy. Existing tokens stay valid until they expire,
+  so also rotate `JWT_SECRET` if a token may have leaked.
+- **Rotating the secret:** replace `JWT_SECRET`; every issued token becomes
+  invalid and every client must sign in again.
+- **CORS** is an explicit allowlist. A missing `Origin` header (curl, a native
+  app) is allowed; any other origin is refused with `403`.
+- **TLS** to Postgres is verified. We do not set `rejectUnauthorized: false`.
+- **Login is rate-limited** to 20 attempts per 15 minutes per address, separately
+  from the 200-request data quota.
+- **Deletes are not exposed.** There is no `DELETE` route; history is append-only.
+
+Never commit `.env`, and never paste a real secret into a README, a screenshot or
+an issue — this repository is public.
